# Git LFS Configuration Template for EXPORTS Folder
#
# This file provides recommended Git LFS tracking patterns for the EXPORTS/ folder
# in the AMPEL360 ASSETS structure.
#
# USAGE:
# ------
# To apply these patterns to your repository:
#
# 1. Ensure Git LFS is installed:
#    git lfs install
#
# 2. Append these patterns to your repository's .gitattributes file:
#    cat .gitattributes-EXPORTS-TEMPLATE >> .gitattributes
#
#    OR manually add the patterns below to your .gitattributes file.
#
# 3. Track existing files (if any):
#    git add .gitattributes
#    git commit -m "Configure Git LFS for EXPORTS folder"
#
# 4. For already-committed large files, migrate them to LFS:
#    git lfs migrate import --include="OPT-IN_FRAMEWORK/**/ASSETS/EXPORTS/**/*.pdf"
#    git lfs migrate import --include="OPT-IN_FRAMEWORK/**/ASSETS/EXPORTS/**/*.png"
#
# WHY USE GIT LFS FOR EXPORTS:
# ----------------------------
# - Exported files (PDF/PNG) are binary and can be large (>1 MB common, >10 MB possible)
# - These files change infrequently but take up significant repository space
# - Git LFS stores them externally while keeping repository clone fast
# - Ideal for distribution-ready outputs that are regenerated from sources
#
# PATTERNS:
# ---------
# This template shows two approaches:
# 1. General patterns (lines 37-40): Apply LFS tracking to ALL EXPORTS folders
# 2. Specific patterns (lines 62-74): Apply LFS tracking only to specific ATA chapters
#
# RECOMMENDATION: Use EITHER general patterns OR specific patterns, not both.
# - For most repositories: Use general patterns (simpler, covers all ATA chapters)
# - For granular control: Comment out general patterns and use specific patterns only

# OPTION 1: General patterns (RECOMMENDED for simplicity)
# Track all PDF files in any EXPORTS folder (across all ATA chapters)
OPT-IN_FRAMEWORK/**/ASSETS/EXPORTS/**/*.pdf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Track all PNG files in any EXPORTS folder
OPT-IN_FRAMEWORK/**/ASSETS/EXPORTS/**/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Optional: Track JPG files if used (less common for technical drawings)
# OPT-IN_FRAMEWORK/**/ASSETS/EXPORTS/**/*.jpg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# OPT-IN_FRAMEWORK/**/ASSETS/EXPORTS/**/*.jpeg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Optional: Track SVG exports if large (typically SVG is text-based and small)
# Only enable if SVG exports exceed 1 MB
# OPT-IN_FRAMEWORK/**/ASSETS/EXPORTS/**/*.svg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Optional: Track other binary formats if used
# OPT-IN_FRAMEWORK/**/ASSETS/EXPORTS/**/*.tiff filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# OPT-IN_FRAMEWORK/**/ASSETS/EXPORTS/**/*.bmp filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

#
# OPTION 2: Specific ATA 54 patterns (for granular control)
# ---------------------------------------------------------
# If you need different LFS policies per ATA chapter, comment out the general
# patterns above and uncomment these specific patterns.
# NOTE: These are redundant if general patterns are active.
#

# ATA 54 Assembly Exports
# OPT-IN_FRAMEWORK/T-TECHNOLOGY_AMEDEOPELLICCIA-ON_BOARD_SYSTEMS/A-AIRFRAME/ATA_54-NACELLES_PYLONS/**/ASSETS/EXPORTS/ASSEMBLIES/*.pdf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# ATA 54 Drawing Exports
# OPT-IN_FRAMEWORK/T-TECHNOLOGY_AMEDEOPELLICCIA-ON_BOARD_SYSTEMS/A-AIRFRAME/ATA_54-NACELLES_PYLONS/**/ASSETS/EXPORTS/DRAWINGS/**/*.pdf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# OPT-IN_FRAMEWORK/T-TECHNOLOGY_AMEDEOPELLICCIA-ON_BOARD_SYSTEMS/A-AIRFRAME/ATA_54-NACELLES_PYLONS/**/ASSETS/EXPORTS/DRAWINGS/**/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# ATA 54 Model Exports
# OPT-IN_FRAMEWORK/T-TECHNOLOGY_AMEDEOPELLICCIA-ON_BOARD_SYSTEMS/A-AIRFRAME/ATA_54-NACELLES_PYLONS/**/ASSETS/EXPORTS/MODELS/*.pdf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# OPT-IN_FRAMEWORK/T-TECHNOLOGY_AMEDEOPELLICCIA-ON_BOARD_SYSTEMS/A-AIRFRAME/ATA_54-NACELLES_PYLONS/**/ASSETS/EXPORTS/MODELS/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# ATA 54 Diagram Exports
# OPT-IN_FRAMEWORK/T-TECHNOLOGY_AMEDEOPELLICCIA-ON_BOARD_SYSTEMS/A-AIRFRAME/ATA_54-NACELLES_PYLONS/**/ASSETS/EXPORTS/DIAGRAMS/*.pdf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# OPT-IN_FRAMEWORK/T-TECHNOLOGY_AMEDEOPELLICCIA-ON_BOARD_SYSTEMS/A-AIRFRAME/ATA_54-NACELLES_PYLONS/**/ASSETS/EXPORTS/DIAGRAMS/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

#
# NOTES:
# ------
# - Git applies .gitattributes patterns in order from top to bottom
# - Later patterns can override earlier patterns for the same file
# - More specific patterns take precedence when they match the same file
# - Use /** for recursive matching across all subdirectories
# - The -text flag tells Git to treat these as binary (no line ending conversion)
# - filter=lfs: Use LFS to store the file content
# - diff=lfs: Use LFS diff driver (shows file size changes instead of content diff)
# - merge=lfs: Use LFS merge driver (handles conflicts by file version)
#
# VERIFICATION:
# -------------
# After applying, verify LFS is tracking your files:
#   git lfs ls-files
#
# Check which files will be tracked by LFS:
#   git lfs track
#
# Verify a specific file is tracked:
#   git check-attr filter -- EXPORTS/ASSEMBLIES/54-00-04-A001_ASSY_Nacelle_Primary_Structure.pdf
#   # Expected output: filter: lfs
#
# MIGRATION OF EXISTING FILES:
# ----------------------------
# If you already committed large files to Git before setting up LFS:
#   git lfs migrate import --include="OPT-IN_FRAMEWORK/**/ASSETS/EXPORTS/**/*.pdf,OPT-IN_FRAMEWORK/**/ASSETS/EXPORTS/**/*.png" --everything
#
# WARNING: This rewrites history. Coordinate with team before running.
#
# PERFORMANCE TIPS:
# -----------------
# - Set LFS transfer concurrency for faster uploads/downloads:
#   git config lfs.concurrenttransfers 8
#
# - Use LFS prune to clean up old LFS objects locally:
#   git lfs prune
#
# - Skip LFS downloads for a faster clone (fetch LFS files on demand):
#   GIT_LFS_SKIP_SMUDGE=1 git clone <repo-url>
#   git lfs pull  # When you need the files
#
# STORAGE CONSIDERATIONS:
# -----------------------
# - GitHub LFS: 1 GB storage, 1 GB/month bandwidth included (free tier)
# - GitHub LFS: Paid tiers available for larger projects
# - Self-hosted: Consider using a self-hosted LFS server for unlimited storage
